    "perplexity": {
      "description": "Patterns by Test Card is an electronic release built around spacious, textural compositions and an understated melodic sensibility. The tracklist suggests a compact but immersive set, with pieces such as “Return Parts Rewind,” “The Stockbridge Damper,” and “Lynwood Alleys” hinting at a reflective, mood-driven approach rather than overtly rhythmic club electronics.\n\nReleased on Home Service Recordings, the album fits the label’s interest in carefully presented experimental and ambient-leaning work. Its titles and presentation point toward a listening experience rooted in detail, atmosphere, and subtle movement, with the record likely appealing to listeners drawn to quiet electronic music that emphasizes tone, drift, and precision over flash.",
